# TV Remote UX

When editing TV browse, player, library, or remote CSS, follow [`docs/tv-remote-ux.md`](docs/tv-remote-ux.md).

## Hard rules

1. Every interactive control must be reachable with Up/Down/Left/Right + Select + Back only.
2. Focusables must sit in orthogonal grids/rails (`data-tv-layout`), not diagonal or floating islands.
3. Floating actions (Skip Intro, FABs) need bidirectional `data-tv-nav-*` bridges into the player/page graph. Never rely on geometric search alone.
4. Dialog backdrops must not be focusable — use `data-tv-backdrop` and/or `tabIndex={-1}`.
5. Do not return a silent dead key mid-screen: if an explicit bridge target is `inert`/hidden, wake it (`__zendeTvWakePlayer`) then focus.
6. Prefer `data-tv-initial-focus` / `data-tv-page-entry` for page entry; hide desktop-only controls with `data-tv-hide-control`.
7. Do not introduce mouse-only or hover-only primary actions on TV surfaces.
8. Keep the single pink remote focus ring in `html[data-tv-input="remote"]`; do not invent alternate focus patterns.
